# Baseline screenshots are ~461MB of binary PNGs and are regenerated, not versioned.
# Committing them would permanently bloat history by that much per recapture.
# Regenerating them needs the Vite app from main PLUS this branch's parity/ harness -
# no single checkout has both. Procedure and the integrity manifest: parity/README.md
# The .meta.json files ARE committed - they are small and are the SEO reference
# (title/meta/canonical/JSON-LD) that the migration must preserve, so they belong in
# code review.
parity/baseline/**/*.png

# Agent worktrees (scratch, per-agent isolation)
.claude/worktrees/

# Next build output
.next/
next-env.d.ts

# TypeScript incremental build cache - regenerated by every typecheck
*.tsbuildinfo
